 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey! How are you feeling?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.35,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_23"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Honestly, a little stressed, but okay.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_07"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My goal this year is one single pull-up. I can't do even half of one.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 0.46,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Great goal. Start with dead hangs, just hanging from the bar for as long as you can.",
   "est_sec": 5.37,
   "gap_before": 1.17,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Just hanging? That's it?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 1.25,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It builds grip and shoulder strength. Then add negatives, jump up to the top and lower yourself as slowly as you can.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How slow?",
   "est_sec": 0.72,
   "gap_before": 0.56,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Aim for three to five seconds on the way down. Do a few sets, two or three times a week.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.56,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "And rows, right? My trainer said something about rows",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.62,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "but I forgot.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.88,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes, rows build the same back muscles. Inverted rows under a table or a bar are a good start.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.92,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay. One pull-up by summer.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.17,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Very realistic with that plan.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.32,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg8"
  }
